SUMMARY:Little Shop of Horrors
DESCRIPTION:Howard Ashman and Alan Menken gave the world this camp classic in 1982. They based the musical (loosely) on the low-budget 1960 black comedy film The Little Shop of Horrors\, with Menken’s score featuring spectacular music: early 1960s-style rock and roll\, doo-wop\, and early Motown. \nThe story centers on meek floral assistant Seymour Krelborn\, who stumbles across a new breed of plant he names “Audrey II” after his coworker crush. This foul-mouthed\, R&B-singing carnivore promises unending fame and fortune to the down-and-out Krelborn as long as he keeps feeding it BLOOD. Over time\, though\, Seymour discovers Audrey II’s out-of-this-world origins and its intent toward global domination! \nJune 26\, 27\, 28; July 2*\, 3\, 5\, 9\, 10\, 11\, 12\nFriday and Saturday Shows: 7:30 PM\nSunday Matinee: 2:00 PM\n*Value Thursday: 7:30 PM \nAdults: $40\nStudent w/ID: $10\n*Special Value Thursday Performance:  Pay What You Can \nBook and Lyrics by Howard Ashman\nMusic By Alan Menken \nDirector                  Katie Watts-Whitaker\nMusic Director        Kelly Considine\nChoreographer       Katie Watts-Whitaker
URL:https://golocal.coop/event/little-shop-of-horrors/2026-07-05/
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater\, 115 North Street\, Healdsburg\, 95448
CATEGORIES:Comedy,Dance Performance,Theater
END:VEVENT
